== Part A: toy note section 6
heading (line 159): '**Shown** (each by executed code):'
  Shown item 1: Model I: an explicit Sp(2,ℝ) ∋ ρ symmetric action with η = ωK as order parameter, including the twisted-ρ caveat.
  Shown item 2: Model I: the instability of the naive ρ-preserving potential, and a bounded, stable replacement.
  Shown item 3: Model I: an ordered ℤ₂ phase in the frozen-H reduction in 1+1.
  Shown item 4: Model II: the explicit matrix-base form of the duality.
  Shown item 5: Model II: complex fields — classical breaking along a flat polarization angle, and restoration under quantization.
  Shown item 6: Model II: real fields — discrete vacua whose classical degeneracy is lifted at one loop in favour of the position-sharp one.
  Shown item 7: In model I and complex model II, ρ sits inside a continuous U(1), so the polarization is a Goldstone angle.
